      "title": "🔓 [Outside Online] With Blood on Her Face and Monkeys Overhead, Erin Ton Just Smashed the Kilimanjaro Speed Record",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/kili-1.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/kili-1.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/kili-1.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/kili-1.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<figure><img alt=\"With Blood on Her Face and Monkeys Overhead, Erin Ton Just Smashed the Kilimanjaro Speed Record\" src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/kili-1.jpg?width=1200\" /></figure>\n<p>rail runner Erin Ton set a new Kilimanjaro FKT, completing the 26.38-mile climb in 8 hours, 33 minutes as part of her Seven Summits speed record project.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.outsideonline.com/outdoor-adventure/hiking-and-backpacking/erin-ton-kilimanjaro-fkt/\">With Blood on Her Face and Monkeys Overhead, Erin Ton Just Smashed the Kilimanjaro Speed Record</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.outsideonline.com\">Outside Online</a>.</p>",
